{"title":"Valentin Vornicu","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Valentin Vornicu</b> is a former <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Art_of_Problem_Solving\" title=\"Art of Problem Solving\">Art of Problem Solving</a> administrator and webmaster.  In 2002, he founded <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MathLinks\" title=\"MathLinks\">MathLinks</a>, which merged with AoPS in 2004.\n</p><p>Vornicu is a multiple time participant in the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a> for Romania.\n</p><p>In 2006, Vornicu graduated from the University of Bucharest, and in 2008 he got his Masters degree in Algebra and Number Theory from the University of Bucharest.\n</p><p>He was a coordinator for the IMO in 2005, 2006 and in 2008. He is also an instructor for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=WOOT\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"WOOT\">WOOT</a>.\n</p><p>Vornicu also has 9 World Series of Poker gold rings and is currently the 486th ranked poker player in the world.\n</p><p>Vornicu currently resides in San Diego.\n</p>\n<div class=\"noprint\" style=\"white-space: nowrap; float: right;\"></div>\n<table class=\"messagebox standard-talk\" id=\"wikipedianarticle\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><i>The subject of this article, <b>Valentin Vornicu</b>, has edited the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS_Wiki\" title=\"AoPS Wiki\">AoPS Wiki</a> as <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Valentin_Vornicu&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Valentin Vornicu (page does not exist)\">Valentin Vornicu</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User_talk:Valentin_Vornicu&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User talk:Valentin Vornicu (page does not exist)\">talk</a> • <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Special:Contributions/Valentin_Vornicu\" title=\"Special:Contributions/Valentin Vornicu\">contribs</a>).</i>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017192449\nCach